{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B9hjb1CWDFAKgD6m5qAz1n","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: prd031-sha1sum\n     2→title: \"cmd/sha1sum: Compute and Check SHA-1 Message Digests\"\n     3→\n     4→problem: |\n     5→  macOS ships shasum rather than sha1sum; the output format and flag set differ from GNU\n     6→  sha1sum. Scripts that generate or verify SHA-1 checksums using the GNU format cannot\n     7→  use the macOS native binary without wrapper adjustments. The Go implementation must\n     8→  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gsha1sum, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte\n     9→  on all flag combinations, using crypto/sha1 from the Go standard library, verified by\n    10→  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n    11→\n    12→goals:\n    13→  - G1: Compute SHA-1 digests for one or more files or stdin and print them in GNU format, matching gsha1sum behavior.\n    14→  - G2: Support --check (-c) to verify a checksum file and report mismatches.\n    15→  - G3: Support --binary (-b), --text (-t), and --tag output format flags.\n    16→\n    17→requirements:\n    18→  R1:\n    19→    title: Digest computation\n    20→    items:\n    21→      - R1.1: Must compute the SHA-1 digest of each named file and write one line per file in the format \"HASH  FILENAME\" (text mode) or \"HASH *FILENAME\" (binary mode). The default is text mode.\n    22→      - R1.2: Must read from stdin and print \"HASH  -\" when no file arguments are given or when \"-\" is provided as a filename.\n    23→      - R1.3: --tag must use BSD-style output format \"SHA1 (FILENAME) = HASH\".\n    24→      - R1.4: Must exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n    25→\n    26→  R2:\n    27→    title: Checksum verification (--check, -c)\n    28→    items:\n    29→      - R2.1: \"--check FILE must read FILE, parse each line (GNU or BSD tag format), recompute the digest, and compare to the stored hash.\"\n    30→      - R2.2: 'Must print \"FILENAME: OK\" or \"FILENAME: FAILED\" for each entry. Must exit 1 if any check fails.'\n    31→      - R2.3: --warn prints a warning for each malformed line. --quiet suppresses OK lines. --status suppresses all output.\n    32→\n    33→  R3:\n    34→    title: Binary and text mode flags\n    35→    items:\n    36→      - R3.1: -b marks input as binary; output uses \"HASH *FILENAME\". -t (default) uses \"HASH  FILENAME\". On Linux/macOS, no functional difference for digest computation.\n    37→      - R3.2: --tag produces BSD tag format regardless of -b/-t.\n    38→\n    39→  R4:\n    40→    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    41→    items:\n    42→      - R4.1: Must exit 0 when all files are processed and all verified digests match.\n    43→      - R4.2: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, any digest fails, or the checksum file is unreadable.\n    44→      - R4.3: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n    45→\n    46→non_goals:\n    47→  - cmd/sha1sum does not implement HMAC-SHA1 or keyed variants.\n    48→  - SHA-1 is cryptographically broken; this implementation is for compatibility with GNU tools only.\n    49→\n    50→acceptance_criteria:\n    51→  - \"AC1: sha1sum on a known file produces the correct SHA-1 hash in GNU format, matching gsha1sum.\"\n    52→  - \"AC2: sha1sum --check on a valid checksum file exits 0 and prints 'FILENAME: OK' for each entry.\"\n    53→  - \"AC3: sha1sum --check on a file with a mismatch exits 1 and prints 'FILENAME: FAILED'.\"\n    54→  - \"AC4: Differential test against gsha1sum passes for all required test cases.\"\n    55→  - \"AC5: cmd/sha1sum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    56→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a39c2daa-64d0-494a-8cfd-c05281f49680","uuid":"8f47ef6a-665e-43bf-a18a-51d2aaba19c9","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/375/docs/specs/product-requirements/prd031-sha1sum.yaml","content":"id: prd031-sha1sum\ntitle: \"cmd/sha1sum: Compute and Check SHA-1 Message Digests\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships shasum rather than sha1sum; the output format and flag set differ from GNU\n  sha1sum. Scripts that generate or verify SHA-1 checksums using the GNU format cannot\n  use the macOS native binary without wrapper adjustments. The Go implementation must\n  match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gsha1sum, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte\n  on all flag combinations, using crypto/sha1 from the Go standard library, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Compute SHA-1 digests for one or more files or stdin and print them in GNU format, matching gsha1sum behavior.\n  - G2: Support --check (-c) to verify a checksum file and report mismatches.\n  - G3: Support --binary (-b), --text (-t), and --tag output format flags.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Digest computation\n    items:\n      - R1.1: Must compute the SHA-1 digest of each named file and write one line per file in the format \"HASH  FILENAME\" (text mode) or \"HASH *FILENAME\" (binary mode). The default is text mode.\n      - R1.2: Must read from stdin and print \"HASH  -\" when no file arguments are given or when \"-\" is provided as a filename.\n      - R1.3: --tag must use BSD-style output format \"SHA1 (FILENAME) = HASH\".\n      - R1.4: Must exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Checksum verification (--check, -c)\n    items:\n      - R2.1: \"--check FILE must read FILE, parse each line (GNU or BSD tag format), recompute the digest, and compare to the stored hash.\"\n      - R2.2: 'Must print \"FILENAME: OK\" or \"FILENAME: FAILED\" for each entry. Must exit 1 if any check fails.'\n      - R2.3: --warn prints a warning for each malformed line. --quiet suppresses OK lines. --status suppresses all output.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Binary and text mode flags\n    items:\n      - R3.1: -b marks input as binary; output uses \"HASH *FILENAME\". -t (default) uses \"HASH  FILENAME\". On Linux/macOS, no functional difference for digest computation.\n      - R3.2: --tag produces BSD tag format regardless of -b/-t.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R4.1: Must exit 0 when all files are processed and all verified digests match.\n      - R4.2: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, any digest fails, or the checksum file is unreadable.\n      - R4.3: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/sha1sum does not implement HMAC-SHA1 or keyed variants.\n  - SHA-1 is cryptographically broken; this implementation is for compatibility with GNU tools only.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - \"AC1: sha1sum on a known file produces the correct SHA-1 hash in GNU format, matching gsha1sum.\"\n  - \"AC2: sha1sum --check on a valid checksum file exits 0 and prints 'FILENAME: OK' for each entry.\"\n  - \"AC3: sha1sum --check on a file with a mismatch exits 1 and prints 'FILENAME: FAILED'.\"\n  - \"AC4: Differential test against gsha1sum passes for all required test cases.\"\n  - \"AC5: cmd/sha1sum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":56}}}
